					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-513338#post-1492650</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-513338/scp-mlp-dnc#post-1492650</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 28 Jun 2012 05:18:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Edrobot</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>413055</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's not that I mind this kind of commentary, it's just that I've seen it done so much better and this doesn't really contribute anything.</p> <p>Speaking of beating a dead horse- erm, pony&#8230;</p> <blockquote> <p>Suddenly, a blue police box appeared in the Head's office. Moments later, a handsome brown colt with an hourglass-shaped cutie mark emerged from the box. &quot;Sorry to bug you, but the multiverse is in grave peril! The Changeling Queen and the Cyberponies have teamed up with Darkseid to start the eighth Holy Grail War! If we don't find the Infinity Gauntlet Philosopher's Stone Equation before they do-&quot;</p> <p><em>&quot;No.&quot;</em> said the department head.</p> <p>&quot;You don't understand!&quot; said Doctor Whooves. &quot;The fate of the entire galaxy rests in our hooves, and only Dr. Clef is a bad enough dude to-&quot;</p> <p><em>&quot;No.&quot;</em></p> <p>&quot;But-&quot;</p> <p><strong><em>&quot;NO.&quot;</em></strong></p> <p>Doctor Whooves shook his head. &quot;You know what? Fine. You win! I'll just go and get one of those Homestuck kids instead. You guys are no fun, anyway. No fun at all.&quot; The pony then went back into his blue box, which dissipeared seconds later.</p> <p>&quot;Good riddance.&quot; said the department head.</p> </blockquote> <p>Actually in all seriousness, I would like to see a crossover with <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/FanFic/TheConversionBureau?from=Main.TheConversionBureau">The Conversion Bureau</a>. No matter how terrible it turns out.</p> <p>Or a Doctor Who fic where Lord Blackwood is his companion.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-513338#post-1492614</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-513338/scp-mlp-dnc#post-1492614</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 28 Jun 2012 04:26:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Gargus</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>588771</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's more of a commentary on general crossovers with the Foundation, with fan-fiction being both an explanation for how it happened and a reference to Shebleha's pushing of the idea.</p> <p>But if you don't like it, feel free to.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-513338#post-1492604</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-513338/scp-mlp-dnc#post-1492604</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 28 Jun 2012 04:14:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Edrobot</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>413055</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>You see it's funny because you're using a fanfiction cliche and very dryly pointing out it is overused.</p> <p>Oh wait no, that's not very funny at all. It's just dull.</p> <p>Now don't get me wrong, I love poking fun at fanfiction cliches (hell, <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Fanfic/ThoseLackingSpines">Those Lacking Spines</a> is my second favorite Kingdom Hearts fic ever), but this is just kind of bland.</p> <p>-1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
